---
// /brick-choir/quartet — Brick Choir 4: Quartet. Four players around one keyboard, four corners of one stage,
// one glass monument in the middle. The keyboard is a map of the screen: each corner of keys is a seat, and each
// seat carries a part of the arrangement (P1 bass, P2 keys, P3 lead, P4 bells; the modifier keys are drum pads).
// Every key fires a ball of light at the monument; every brick is a note; each key owns a column of its face.
// The song passes seat to seat: the glowing brick calls a corner, that corner answers, the choir echoes.
// Balls that get inside play runs, the hollow core is a bell, a face clear is a fanfare, four seats in one beat is
// a QUARTET. Empty seats are friendly bots, so it is a solo instrument and a couch co-op game at once.
// Rounds by the Architects (Terra, Sonnet, Astra) rebuilt as ziggurats. three.js 0.170 (pinned, jsDelivr).
// ?attract → silent, input-free attract mode for the lobby cabinet at /brick-choir (throttled when unfocused).
// Scores post with game:"quartet"; the board opens on THIS WEEK with an ALL TIME toggle; SHARE at game over
// publishes the run to /api/keyboard and draws a share card. Built 2026-09-23 by Claude (Fable) for Mike.
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
